# Direct Python dependencies for the transcribe and summarize stages.
#
# This is the file you edit. The pinned, hash-checked `requirements.txt` beside
# it is generated from it and is what setup.sh actually installs — so two boxes
# set up months apart get byte-identical SDK versions instead of whatever PyPI
# was serving that week. That drift is not hypothetical: an SDK that quietly
# changes its request surface is how `budget_tokens` turned into a 400 on every
# summarize call.
#
# Regenerate after editing (needs uv — see README's Install section):
#
#     uv pip compile --generate-hashes requirements.in -o requirements.txt
#     uv pip compile --generate-hashes -c requirements.txt \
#         requirements-browser.in -o requirements-browser.txt
#
# The `-c requirements.txt` on the second one keeps shared transitive deps at
# the same versions in both files.
#
# Resolved for the deployment target: CPython 3.13 on linux-x86_64 (Debian 13).
# A different target needs its own recompile.

# No anthropic SDK: the default summary backend runs the `claude` CLI as a
# subprocess so the summary is billed to the operator's Claude subscription
# rather than to a metered API key. The CLI is installed by claude.ai/install.sh,
# not by pip — see README's Install section.
#
# The fallback summary backend.
google-genai
# youtube-transcript.io client. urllib gets rate-limited on that endpoint where
# requests does not — different User-Agent and TLS stack.
requests
# Pre-recorded transcription for local files.
assemblyai
# The PDF export: markdown -> HTML -> PDF, and the frame cropping.
weasyprint
markdown
pillow
